  "summary": "Summer has sprung\nMemorial Day brought in the unofficial start to Summer 2013 in the United States, a line of demarcation that has historically meant increased driving by American families. The American consumer has been demanding less and less motor gasoline, though, as increasing vehicle efficiency standards and higher prices have dampened and then reversed decades' worth of demand growth. A Wall Street Journal piece by Liam Denning noted earlier this week that \"Bureau of Economic Analysis energy economist Phil Verleger calculates that fixed costs such as rent, loan payments and medical insurance now swallow more than 80% of total consumer expenditures.",
